    "body": "---\nname: \"repeater\"\ndescription: \"Sending PoCs to Burp Suite Repeater via MCP\"\nversion: \"1.0.0\"\nauthor: \"burp-ai (ported)\"\ntags: [\"pentest\", \"utility\", \"repeater\"]\ntrigger_patterns:\n  - \"/repeater\"\n  - \"use burp repeater\"\n  - \"replay requests\"\n---\n\n# Sending PoCs to Burp Suite Repeater via MCP\n\nThis guide explains how to use the Burp Suite MCP tools to send proof-of-concept requests to Repeater.\n\n## Basic Repeater Tab Creation\n\nUse the `repeater_tab` tool to create a new Repeater tab with a raw HTTP request.\n\n### Required Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n|-----------|------|-------------|\n| `content` | string | The raw HTTP request (must use `\\r\\n` line endings) |\n| `targetHostname` | string | The target host (without protocol) |\n| `targetPort` | integer | Port number (80 for HTTP, 443 for HTTPS) |\n| `usesHttps` | boolean | `true` for HTTPS, `false` for HTTP |\n\n### Optional Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n|-----------|------|-------------|\n| `tabName` | string | Custom name for the Repeater tab |\n\n## Example: Basic GET Request\n\n```json\n{\n  \"content\": \"GET /path HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: example.com\\r\\nCookie: session=abc123\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\n  \"targetHostname\": \"example.com\",\n  \"targetPort\": 443,\n  \"usesHttps\": true,\n  \"tabName\": \"My PoC\"\n}\n```\n\n## Example: POST Request with Body\n\n```json\n{\n  \"content\": \"POST /api/login HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: example.com\\r\\nContent-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\\r\\nContent-Length: 27\\r\\n\\r\\nusername=admin&password=test\",\n  \"targetHostname\": \"example.com\",\n  \"targetPort\": 443,\n  \"usesHttps\": true,\n  \"tabName\": \"Login PoC\"\n}\n```\n\n## Key Points\n\n1. **Line Endings**: HTTP requests require CRLF (`\\r\\n`) line endings. The request must end with a blank line (`\\r\\n\\r\\n` after headers, or after body if present).\n\n2. **Host Header**: Always include the `Host` header matching your target.\n\n3. **Content-Length**: For POST/PUT requests with a body, include the correct `Content-Length` header.\n\n4. **HTTPS**: Set `usesHttps: true` and `targetPort: 443` for HTTPS targets.\n\n## Repeater Tab with Payload Replacement\n\nUse `repeater_tab_with_payload` to create a tab with placeholder substitutions:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"content\": \"GET /search?q={{PAYLOAD}} HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: example.com\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\n  \"replacements\": {\n    \"{{PAYLOAD}}\": \"<script>alert(1)</script>\"\n  },\n  \"targetHostname\": \"example.com\",\n  \"targetPort\": 443,\n  \"usesHttps\": true,\n  \"tabName\": \"XSS Test\"\n}\n```\n\n## Common Use Cases\n\n### SQL Injection PoC\n```json\n{\n  \"content\": \"GET /product?id=1' OR '1'='1 HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: target.com\\r\\nCookie: session=xyz\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\n  \"targetHostname\": \"target.com\",\n  \"targetPort\": 443,\n  \"usesHttps\": true,\n  \"tabName\": \"SQLi PoC\"\n}\n```\n\n### XSS PoC\n```json\n{\n  \"content\": \"GET /search?q=<script>alert(document.domain)</script> HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: target.com\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\n  \"targetHostname\": \"target.com\",\n  \"targetPort\": 443,\n  \"usesHttps\": true,\n  \"tabName\": \"XSS PoC\"\n}\n```\n\n### SSRF PoC\n```json\n{\n  \"content\": \"POST /api/fetch HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: target.com\\r\\nContent-Type: application/json\\r\\nContent-Length: 42\\r\\n\\r\\n{\\\"url\\\":\\\"http://169.254.169.254/latest/\\\"}\",\n  \"targetHostname\": \"target.com\",\n  \"targetPort\": 443,\n  \"usesHttps\": true,\n  \"tabName\": \"SSRF PoC\"\n}\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n- **Request not sending**: Ensure the request ends with `\\r\\n\\r\\n`\n- **Connection errors**: Verify `targetHostname`, `targetPort`, and `usesHttps` match the target\n- **Malformed request**: Check that headers are properly formatted with `\\r\\n` between each"
